    "english":  "By pushing my golden bangles back onto my forearms,\nI hid from my mother\u0027s eyes how thin my wrists have grown;\nand when my plaited hair was disheveled in play with my companions,\nI excused the exhaustion of my body as mere games.\nYet how can I hide the telltale tears that fill my eyes\nevery time I look upon the path through the mountain woods?\nLike the blue neytal blossoms that lose their morning brilliance\nin the salt marshes of Korkai, famous for its pearl-yielding seas,\nmy eyes have lost their luster through love\u0027s unyielding sorrow,\nand the secret ache of my heart can no longer be concealed!",
